    "text_full": "Paris Buttfield-Addison\nTechnology · Policy · Games · Arts · Education · Writing\nEVENTS\nWRITING\nABOUT\nPOSTS\n01\nParis Buttfield-Addison\nHi! I’m a computer scientist, game designer, writer, artist, and technical product leader based in Hobart. I work at the intersection of technology, policy, and human behaviour. I co-founded Secret Lab, the indie studio behind BAFTA-winning Night in the Woods and the ABC Play School games. I also co-founded Yarn Spinner, narrative tools used in thousands of games played by millions including DREDGE, A Short Hike, and Venba.\n\nI’ve written over 20 technical books on AI, machine learning, and software development. I’m completing a law degree because I wanted to understand how regulation works, particularly for AI. I do independent research on AI governance, analysing gaps between policy, law, and how people actually behave when using these systems.\n\nI help run /dev/world (longest-running Apple developer event not run by Apple, since 2008), serve as President of Tasmanian Game Makers, and host a radio show on space news. I’ve worked at Meebo (acquired by Google) and delivered keynotes and workshops worldwide.\n\nLearn more about me. My amazing wife Mars is here.\n02\nRecent Posts\nAPR 2026\nLibraries Tasmania Research Fellowship\nAPR 2026\nBig Plans is out now\nAPR 2026\nSpace News, April 2026\nMAR 2026\nSpace News, March 2026\nFEB 2026\nThe New Try Yarn Spinner\nFEB 2026\nTas Game Makers 2026\nFEB 2026\nSpace News, February 2026\nJAN 2026\nWe Made a Game About a 1993 Hint Line\nJAN 2026\nState of Play: How Australian States Are (Not) Governing AI\nVIEW ALL POSTS →\n03\nElsewhere\nMASTODON\nBLUESKY\nTHREADS\nINSTAGRAM\nFLICKR\nGITHUB\nFACEBOOK\nLINKEDIN\n\n© 2026 Dr Paris Buttfield-Addison · Privacy"
